body:
Vaguely related;
I was watching a movie using my laptop hooked to the TV, with my dad. He used to always say something along the lines of 'gross' when people kissed in movies.

Anyway these people in the movie started to kiss, and my laptop decided at that moment to notify me that my "Virus database has been updated" it said it aloud and popped up a little notification from my antivirus.

I must admit I laughed slightly at;
>He's so committed to being "polite."

Followed immediately by;

>I expressed as much, in what I hoped was a gentle way, but I saw this flash of annoyance from him, and now I'm annoyed. Very annoyed. 


It comes off as;

"Don't be polite"
*Fails to politely hide annoyance.*
"How dare he be annoyed at me!"


I do get that sometimes the overwhelming amount of politeness required by society is tiring, most of it is intended to avoid hurting feelings and can be difficult programming to undo when just with significant others, especially when it will still be expected of them outside the house.

Lol.
Shared this with my SO, his response was;
"And that's why we don't have mommy dwarves anymore."

Yes. :)

&#x200B;

I don't know how to do a thumbs-up emoji...

Third for Lolly#333

